  <div class="side-text"><div class="text"><p>A single-color <strong><em>ultraviolet</em></strong> variant of NeoPixel strip is available for special applications, currently one pixel density and backing color:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="../www.adafruit.com/product/3851"><strong>32 UV LEDs per meter, white strip</strong></a></li>
</ul>
<p>This can provide unusual effects when combined with UV-reactive paints, fluorescent laser-cut acrylic, etc.</p>
<p>The usual NeoPixel R, G and B channels translate to three individual UV diodes. So we recommend you pretty much just set all three channels to the same value, ranging from (0, 0, 0) to (255, 255, 255).</p>
<p>Same width as “classic” NeoPixel strip, and power draw at full brightness should be just a bit more than RGB 30/m: about 9.6W/meter (1.9A @ 5V).</p></div></div>
