  </div>

    </div>
  <div class="side-text"><div class="text"><p>This 5x8 <strong><a href="../www.adafruit.com/products/1430">NeoPixel Shield for Arduino</a></strong> fits neatly atop an Arduino Uno or compatible boards (5V logic recommended). Like many of our NeoPixel products, they’re available in <strong>RGB</strong> and various <strong>RGBW</strong> pixel types:</p>
<h2><strong><a href="../www.adafruit.com/product/3053">NeoPixel Shield Product Selector</a></strong></h2>
<p> </p>
<p>By default, the LEDs are powered from the Arduino’s 5V pin. As long as you <em>aren't</em> lighting up all the pixels at full brightness that should be fine. Or power the shield with an external power supply by soldering the included terminal block.</p>
<p>The NeoPixels are controlled on <strong>digital pin 6</strong>, but with some deft wiring you could change this to any pin.</p></div></div>
</div>

