  <div class="side-text"><div class="text"><p>USB power banks can sometimes be used a couple of ways…</p>
<ul>
<li>Powering a microcontroller board through its USB port, tapping power for the NeoPixels from the board’s 5V or VIN pin.</li>
<li>Dissecting a USB cable to provide 5V directly to the pixels.</li>
</ul>
<p>Many USB power banks <strong>shut off automatically</strong> when current draw is low (e.g. few or no pixels lit), so this requires experimentation and isn’t ideal for all situations.</p></div></div>
</div>

